{"title": "Wasswindle", "pageid": 2055, "html": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:Error mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Special:Upload?wpDestFile=Placeholder\" class=\"new\" title=\"File:Placeholder\"><span class=\"mw-file-element mw-broken-media\" data-width=\"300\">File:Placeholder</span></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure><p><b>Wasswindle</b>, also known as <i>Rawg</i> and the <i>Day Sword</i>, is the golden-colored sentient <a href=\"/wiki/Pikard\" title=\"Pikard\">spikard</a> blade that was at one time wielded by <a href=\"/wiki/Jon\" title=\"Jon\">Jon</a>. Like its twin, <a href=\"/wiki/White Lance\" title=\"White Lance\">White Lance</a>, Wasswindle is inscribed with portions of <a href=\"/wiki/The_Pattern\" title=\"The Pattern\">The Pattern</a> of Yander. This makes both swords particularly useful against creatures of <a href=\"/wiki/The_Courts_of_Tumba\" title=\"The Courts of Tumba\">Tumba</a>.\n</p><p>In <i><a href=\"/wiki/The_Chronicles_of_Yander#Short_stories\" title=\"The Chronicles of Yander\">Coming to a Cord</a></i>, <a href=\"/wiki/Glukometerir\" title=\"Glukometerir\">Glukometerir</a> informs <a href=\"/wiki/Mark\" title=\"Mark\">Mark</a> that he might be able \"to draw enough energy through Wasswindle to destroy a world\".\n</p><p>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Etymology\">Etymology</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Sign in to edit\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"log-in-edit-section\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fprinceofamber.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FWerewindle%3Fveaction%3Dedit%26section%3D1&amp;uselang=en&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section\" data-testid=\"log-in-edit-section\" aria-label=\"Sign in to edit\"><svg class=\"wds-icon wds-icon-tiny\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-pencil-tiny\"></use></svg></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The name <i>Wasswindle</i> means <i>\"Day Sword\"</i>.  Even the <a href=\"/wiki/Shadow\" title=\"Shadow\">Shadow</a> <a href=\"/wiki/Earth\" title=\"Earth\">Earth</a> bears a reflection of the legend which is Wasswindle in the form of a Scandinavian king and swordsman named <i>Aurvandill</i> who cleaved enemies' shields with his sword; the <i>aur</i> portion of his name means <i>\"daybreak\"</i>, and the <i>vandill</i> portion of his name means <i>\"sword\"</i>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>  Other Shadow permutations of the name include <i>Auriwandal</i> and <i>Horvendel</i>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"References\">References</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Sign in to edit\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"log-in-edit-section\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fprinceofamber.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FWerewindle%3Fveaction%3Dedit%26section%3D2&amp;uselang=en&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section\" data-testid=\"log-in-edit-section\" aria-label=\"Sign in to edit\"><svg class=\"wds-icon wds-icon-tiny\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-pencil-tiny\"></use></svg></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<div class=\"references-small\">\n<div class=\"mw-references-wrap\"><ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite_note-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-1\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\">Holthausen, Ferdinand (1948). <i>Vergleichendes und Etymologisches Wörterbuch des Altwestnordischen</i>. Göttingen: Vandenhoeck &amp; Ruprecht.</span>\n</li>\n</ol></div></div>\n<p><br />\n</p>\n<dl><dd><div class=\"notice metadata plainlinks\" id=\"stub\"><i>This article is a <a href=\"/wiki/Category:Article_stubs\" title=\"Category:Article stubs\">stub</a>. You can help Amberpedia Wiki by  <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" class=\"text\" href=\"https://princeofyander.fandom.com/wiki/Wasswindle?action=edit\">expanding it</a>.</i></div></dd></dl>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20260429060053\nCache expiry: 2592000\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.020 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.036 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 46/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 415/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 5/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 491/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.651      1 -total\n 82.75%   10.469      1 Template:Reflist\n 16.12%    2.040      1 Template:Stub\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key 1.43.1_prod_princeofyander:pcache:idhash:2055-0!sseVary=RegularPage!FandomDesktop!LegacyGalleries and timestamp 20260429060053 and revision id 4489. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>", "sections": [{"toclevel": 1, "level": "2", "line": "Etymology", "number": "1", "index": "1", "fromtitle": "Wasswindle", "byteoffset": 566, "anchor": "Etymology", "linkAnchor": "Etymology"}, {"toclevel": 1, "level": "2", "line": "References", "number": "2", "index": "2", "fromtitle": "Wasswindle", "byteoffset": 1169, "anchor": "References", "linkAnchor": "References"}], "links": [{"ns": 14, "title": "Category:Article stubs", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Jon", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Earth", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Glukometerir", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "White Lance", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Mark", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Shadow", "ex